;; What this case exercises; edit by hand.  `bb corpus-accept' leaves it alone.
(:book "testing_and_staying_sane"
 :source "testing_and_staying_sane.pdf"
 :page 9
 :exercises "Unnumbered bold sub-heads the bold-ok air demand eats.

\"Lessons from the queue example\" is a single CMBX10 line at 1.02
body heights - a face the body never uses - but LNCS sets its
sub-head air at ~1.0-1.1 leadings against the 1.35 the bold-ok test
demands, so five of the paper's seven sub-heads never become
candidates and the CMBX10 cluster never reaches support.  The head
renders as plain prose: wholly bold, so the emphasis whole-line skip
leaves it without even markers.  A non-body face relaxes the air
demand to any positive gap; the full demand keeps guarding the body
face, whose bold labels inside a tight flow are the page's own text.

The numbered sections (CMBX12 at 1.22 body) cluster and render fine
either way - the damage is one level down.

Budget: the q:put listing's output lines pair as lowercase seams,
and one prose paragraph splits at the listing boundary (\"We\" /
\"created\"); QuickCheck is the prose's own camelCase."
 :budget (:mid-sentence 4 :glued 1))
